<title>UK: UAE produced 2.18 million bpd in November - OPECNA.</title>
<headline>UAE produced 2.18 million bpd in November - OPECNA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UAE informed OPEC that it produced 2.18 million barrels per day (bpd) of crude in November, or 20,000 bpd above its OPEC quota, the OPEC news agency OPECNA said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But the UAE's supply to the market was fractionally below its quota of 2.161 million bpd, it told OPEC.</p>
<p>OPEC quotas are based on supply to the market rather than wellhead production.</p>
<p>Supply is defined by OPEC as domestic consumption, plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held abroad.</p>
<p>Production and supply data for November received so far by the OPEC secretariat from member states is as follows (in thousand bpd):</p>
<p>Country				   Production		Supply</p>
<p>Algeria					795.0		  773.0</p>
<p>Indonesia				  1,327.4		1,327.0</p>
<p>Iran					 3,597.0		3,597.0</p>
<p>Iraq					   725.0		  725.0</p>
<p>Kuwait				     2,009.5		2,010.3</p>
<p>Libya					1,400.0		1,400.0</p>
<p>Nigeria				    1,865.0		1,865.0</p>
<p>Qatar					  392.2		  382.3</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia			     8,012.3		8,001.</p>
<p>UAE					  2,181.8		2,159.2</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
